eXcel wrote:
>
> Now, I'm wondering what I should use as a second weapon.

My initial cut at a barbarian weapons skill slot strategy -

Maximum capabilites are:

Restricted - knife, polearm, javelin, lance, sling, crossbow, dart,
shuriken, boomerang, whip, unihorn, martial arts

Basic - dagger, saber, flail, quarterstaff, bow, two weapon, riding

Skilled - pickaxe, broadsword, long sword, scimitar, club, mace,
morning star, spear, trident, attack spells

Expert - axe, short sword, two handed sword, hammer

Master - bare handed

Initial skills are Basic in axe plus (Basic in either short sword or
two handed sword) depending on initial weapons.

Can be Neutral of Chaotic so possible artifacts could include either
Stormy or Mojo.  First gift is Cleaver.


Cost to enhance attack spells to Skilled is 4 - worth it to max them
out.

Cost to advance two weapon to Basic is 1 - worth it.

I waffle on whether Expert is worth it at any time before all other
interesting schools/classes have been enhanced to

Skilled, but this specific discussion is the end game.



I would advance these to Basic - dagger, saber, two weapon, pickaxe - 4
slots leaving 22.

I would advance these to Skilled - Either broadsword (chaotic Stormy)
or long sword (neutral Vorpy) - 3 slots leaving

20.

I would advance attack spells to Skilled - 2 slots leaving 18, and axe
plus the initial short sword or two handed sword

- 4 slots leaving 14.

That leaves a lot of options in the late game.  If Mojo arrives run
hammer to Expert - 6 slots leaving 8.

Axe to Expert for Cleaver (from Skilled above) - 3 slots leaving 5.

This leaves 5 slots to spend on pickaxe to Skilled and/or whatever
artifacts arrive other than the ones mentioned above.

 If both broadsword and long sword artifacts arrive max them both at 3
each and have 2 to spare on other artifacts.

I think it might be worth enhancing bow to Basic costing one slot to
have the choice of two different single shot

missile attacks.  Since barbarians can get to Skilled in attack spells
their firing order appears to be spell, missile,

melee without including polearm.  The number of spells before switching
to throwing daggers would be limited by the

energy and food supplies.

I think a barbarian should end up two weaponing Stormy or Mojo or Vorpy
or Frosty or some other artifact with a silver saber.  Keep a bunch of
daggers to throw even if they are only thrown one per turn.  Maybe a
bow as a backup missile attack.  Have an assortment of wands.  And
start casting every known attack spell as soon as an advancing monster
is seen.  This means attention should be spent on increasing stats to
make spell casting lower failure plus leveling up for lower failure,
plus maxing luck for all types of attack.



